    {
      "id": "code-review-ppt-web-toast-announcer-provider-value-not-memoized",
      "action": "ppt-web Toast and Announcer context providers pass a fresh object literal as `value` on every render (Toast.tsx:199 `{ showToast, removeToast }`, Announcer.tsx:96 `{ announce }`), forcing all consumers to re-render. Both members are already useCallback-stable, so wrap each provider `value` in `useMemo`. Same symptom class as the org-provider finding (merged #3514); these two were out-of-scope there.",
      "owner_role": "pm-frontend",
      "priority": "low",
